diagnosis: switches to turn off piecewise commit and the loop suspend check

Three environment variables, read once when a program starts, that put back how things were
before a FineWine change, so that a problem can be pinned on one of them (or cleared of them)
by starting the program again, without another build:

 - FEX_EAGERCOMMIT=1: the lookup tables are committed whole at their first fault (0005), the
   allocator commits each page whole (0006), and call-return stacks and compile buffers are
   committed whole (0007).
 - FEX_NOLOOPSUSPENDCHECK=1: no suspend check before a conditional jump back (0004). A program
   that suspends a thread spinning in such a loop then hangs again, as Genshin Impact did.

They cost memory or hang programs, so they are for finding a fault only. The Wine side has
FINEWINE_EAGER_CODE_MAP=1 for the ARM64EC code map (runtime patch 0037).

